From 77209500a6ccbdb7b72374ad5ad0fd3aba056eb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-v12 <v12@localhost>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 00:33:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] v12: exhaustive regression tests (peepholes, IR, codegen,
 FP, SIMD-adjacent)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Seven new differential tests closing the coverage gaps this session's work
touched (regression suite 134 -> 141):

- v12_flat_short_circuit: flat short-circuit lowering — every nesting shape
  (flat, mixed &&/||, parens), constants in every position, observable
  side effects in every operand slot, eval-order/stop-at-first-decisive.
- v12_range_fold_edges: range-fold + compare-narrowing edge cases (span 0,
  span 255, lo 0, hi 255, signed byte, u16, non-narrowable spans).
- v12_alu_peepholes: LEA strength reduction (x*3/5/9), mul/div/mod by
  constants (signed+unsigned, +/- divisors), identities (x*0, x-x, x&0, ...),
  mul-add fusion, INT_MIN/INT_MAX edges.
- v12_bitops: popcount/clz/ctz/ffs/parity/bswap16/32/64 builtins over
  undefined-input edge values.
- v12_fp_param: runtime FP parameter XMM allocation (F32/F64, 4+ params,
  mixed FP/int), exposed the FP-param pre-store ordering miscompile.
- v12_dead_param: dead parameter store elimination (unused + constant-folded
  params, FP and int).
- v12_alu_chains: GPR simple-ALU LHS hints + fused compare-to-branch chains
  over wrap-sensitive edges.

All bit-exact vs GCC.
