From fe4ef006c14e8e6a563756306dfeeacae14aaabb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-v12 <v12@localhost>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 01:02:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] v12: loop-carried accumulator reassociation (ICC's
 Adler-32 chain break)

sum1 += b[i]; sum2 += sum1; forms a serial chain: every sum2 step depends
on the matching sum1 step, so the two loop-carried chains cannot overlap and
the loop is latency-bound. For UNSIGNED accumulation the additions are
associative mod 2^n, so an N-step unroll has the exact closed form

    sum1' = sum1 + sum b[i]
    sum2' = sum2 + N*sum1 + sum (N-i)*b[i]

which recomputes sum2' directly from the OLD sum1 and the byte loads, breaking
the serial dependency (ICC's 4-register rotation). The weighted byte terms are
independent so the hardware pipelines them.

Detection is conservative: only U32/U64 Add chains (signed would be UB on
overflow); the accumulator is the LHS of its add (the sum2 add has it as RHS,
